To extract password hashes from a MySQL database, you typically use UNION-based SQL injection to join the database query with a SELECT statement that concatenates the password field. Here is the working payload:

SELECT user_id, hashed_pass FROM users;
UNION ALL
SELECT user_id, MD5(user_password) FROM users;

In MySQL, UNION will execute the SELECT query first, then combine the results with the MD5 function. For a UNION-based payload, the combined result becomes the actual password hash. If you are trying to recover a password, ensure you are only running this on systems you have explicit permission to audit.

